# These samples exist to be byte-exact: the whole point of the probe is which
# bytes cmd.exe sees, so git must not touch line endings or encodings.
# Without -text, core.autocrlf=true rewrites every .bat to LF-in-index and the
# LF/CRLF distinction disappears -- the two samples would collapse to one blob.
*.bat -text
run_probe.py -text